#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from using the server-side Sampler and Estimator to the client-side "
"implementations of these primitives in IBM Quantum Compute Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator {#migrate-"
"from-server-side-to-client-side-sampler-and-estimator}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide describes how to migrate from the **server-side** implementations of IBM Quantum&reg;\n"
"`Sampler` and `Estimator` to their new **client-side** implementations in\n"
"`qiskit-ibm-runtime`. The interfaces and options are largely unchanged, so most code\n"
"runs as-is, but there are some behavioral differences to understand.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sampler and Estimator are primitive *interfaces* defined in Qiskit. The IBM Quantum\n"
"Compute Service (formerly Qiskit Runtime) has historically provided the *implementation*\n"
"of these primitives inside its runtime environment. When you call `sampler.run()` or\n"
"`estimator.run()`, the request is sent to the service, and **all** computation — including\n"
"error suppression and mitigation — happens on the server side.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This black-box experience is convenient: you don't have to worry about implementation\n"
"details. But it also makes the primitives hard to debug, customize, or learn from,\n"
"because you can't see what happens during processing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The newly introduced [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model#directed-execution-model-beta) takes the opposite approach and\n"
"provides a **white-box** experience. All design intents are captured on the client side,\n"
"and a single server-side primitive [**Executor**](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive) processes those inputs exactly as\n"
"directed — it makes no implicit decisions on your behalf.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, Sampler and Estimator are re-implemented\n"
"on the **client side** on top of Executor. They provide the same convenience and\n"
"abstraction as before, and now you can inspect the implementation details when you need\n"
"to. Because the interfaces and options remain largely the same, migration should be\n"
"seamless.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note: IBM Quantum only supports version 2 of Sampler and Estimator "
"interfaces (`BaseSamplerV2` and `BaseEstimatorV2`). Therefore, they are "
"simply referred to as Sampler and Estimator in this guide.\n"
msgstr ""

