#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Incompatible changes in the new Sampler {#incompatible-changes-in-the-new-"
"sampler}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Change | Migration action |\n"
"| ------ | ---------------- |\n"
"| The underlying primitive is now Executor. Both the IBM Quantum Platform user interface and `job.primitive_id` will show `executor` instead of `sampler`. | Update any code that references `job.primitive_id`. |\n"
"| The new implementation maps Sampler inputs to Executor inputs, so `job.inputs` returns Executor inputs. | Update any code that references `job.inputs`. See [Job inputs](#job-inputs-structure). |\n"
"| More pre- and post-processing now happens on the client side, so `sampler.run()` and `job.result()` might take longer than before. | Enable INFO logging to follow the progress of client-side processing. See [Enable INFO logging](#enable-info-logging). |\n"
"| Circuit metadata is copied into result metadata. The data types allowed in result metadata are now limited to `str`, `float`, `int`, `bool`, and lists or dictionaries of those types. | If you need other data types, encode them as a string first (for example, with base64). |\n"
"| Options classes (`options_models.SamplerOptions` and so on) are now Pydantic models instead of dataclasses, so they can no longer be converted to Python dictionaries by using `asdict()`. | Use `options.model_dump()` instead. |\n"
"| Options classes that previously had the `V2` suffix (`ExecutionOptionsV2` and so on) no longer do, since V1 primitives are no longer supported. | Remove the `V2` suffix of these options classes: replace `ExecutionOptionsV2` with `ExecutionOptions`, `ResilienceOptionsV2` with `ResilienceOptions`, and `SamplerExecutionOptionsV2` with `SamplerExecutionOptions`. |\n"
"| If `twirling` is enabled and `shots` (in the PUBs or in `run()`), `shots_per_randomization`, and `num_randomizations` are **all** specified, then `num_randomizations * shots_per_randomization` takes precedence over `shots`. | Omit `num_randomizations` and `shots_per_randomization` if you want the `shots` value to be used. |\n"
"| Some input validation has moved to the server side and now raises `RuntimeError` instead of `IBMInputValueError`. | Update the exception types your code catches. |\n"
"| Mixed shot values in a single job are no longer supported. | Submit a separate job for each shot value. See [Job splitting](#job-splitting) for considerations. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Incompatible changes in the new Estimator {#incompatible-changes-in-the-new-"
"estimator}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Change | Migration action |\n"
"| ------ | ---------------- |\n"
"| The underlying primitive is now Executor. Both the IBM Quantum Platform user interface and `job.primitive_id` will show `executor` instead of `estimator`. | Update any code that references `job.primitive_id`. |\n"
"| The new implementation maps Estimator inputs to Executor inputs, so `job.inputs` returns Executor inputs. |Update any code that references `job.inputs`. See [Job inputs](#job-inputs-structure). |\n"
"| More pre- and post-processing now happens on the client side, so `estimator.run()` and `job.result()` might take longer than before. | Enable INFO logging to follow the progress of client-side processing. See [Enable INFO logging](#enable-info-logging). |\n"
"| Circuit metadata is copied into result metadata. The data types allowed in result metadata are now limited to `str`, `float`, `int`, `bool`, and lists or dictionaries of those types. | If you need other data types, encode them as a string first (for example, with base64). |\n"
"| Options classes (`options_models.EstimatorOptions` and so on) are now Pydantic models instead of dataclasses, so they can no longer be converted to Python dictionaries using `asdict()`. | Use `options.model_dump()` instead. |\n"
"| Options classes that have `V2` suffix before (`ExecutionOptionsV2` and so on) no longer do, since V1 primitives are no longer supported. | Remove the `V2` suffix of these options classes: replace `ExecutionOptionsV2` with `ExecutionOptions` and `ResilienceOptionsV2` with `ResilienceOptions`. |\n"
"| All input options are returned in result metadata, rather than a selected subset. | None — this is informational. |\n"
"| Some input validation has moved to the server side and now raises `RuntimeError` instead of `IBMInputValueError`. | Update the exception types your code catches. |\n"
"| No more implicit noise learning for PEA and PEC. Measurement noise learning for TREX is still supported. | Learn the noise models separately and pass them to Estimator. See [Perform explicit noise learning for PEA and PEC](#perform-explicit-noise-learning-for-pea-and-pec). |\n"
"| The input type of `ResilienceOptions.layer_noise_model` is different and can be constructed from `NoiseLearnerV3` results. | See [Perform explicit noise learning for PEA and PEC](#perform-explicit-noise-learning-for-pea-and-pec) on how to learn the noise models using `NoiseLearnerV3` and pass them to Estimator. |\n"
"| `MeasureNoiseLearningOptions.shots_per_randomization` is no longer supported. | A single shot value is used for all circuits in the job, including measurement noise-learning circuits. If you must use a different shot value, apply TREX with `qiskit-mitigation` outside Estimator.|\n"
"| Mixed precision values in a single job are no longer supported. | Submit a separate job for each desired precision. See [Job splitting](#job-splitting) for considerations. |\n"
"| The `seed_estimator` option is no longer supported. | Remove any `options.seed_estimator` assignment (setting it raises a `ValidationError`). There is no client-side equivalent, so results are no longer reproducible through this seed. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enable INFO logging {#enable-info-logging}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because more work now happens on the client side, it's useful to see the progress of that\n"
"processing. Enable INFO-level logging for the `qiskit_ibm_runtime` logger:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Perform explicit noise learning for PEA and PEC {#perform-explicit-noise-"
"learning-for-pea-and-pec}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The new Estimator no longer performs *implicit* noise learning when the PEA or PEC error\n"
"mitigation method is selected. You must learn the noise models explicitly and pass them\n"
"in. Use the new [`NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/noise-learning#noiselearnerv3) to control how circuits\n"
"are stratified into layers. It takes a list of boxed circuit instructions (for example,\n"
"the unique layers) as input.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Important\">\n"
"PEA and PEC now **require** this explicit pattern. Do not skip the noise-learning step\n"
"or your code will fail. Measurement noise learning for TREX is unaffected and continues to work as before.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, if your code uses `NoiseLearner` and passes the resulting noise "
"model to server-side Estimator, you need to [migrate to "
"`NoiseLearnerV3`](/guides/migrate-to-noise-learner-v3). Do NOT use the older"
" `NoiseLearner`, which is incompatible with the new Estimator.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of the noise learning options in the server-side Estimator "
"(`LayerNoiseLearningOptions`) map directly to the `NoiseLearnerV3` option "
"([`NoiseLearnerV3Options`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options)), with the exception of "
"`max_layers_to_learn`. The number of layers to learn is instead based on the"
" number of layers passed to `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
msgstr ""

